  "notes": [
    "* Counted as a tense of the indicative in Spanish and Portuguese.",
    "Portuguese tenho estudado describes a repeated or ongoing action. For a single finished action, where Italian says ho studiato, Portuguese says estudei.",
    "German Präteritum covers both the imperfetto and the passato remoto, and in speech the Perfekt often replaces the passato remoto.",
    "In hypothetical clauses German uses the Konjunktiv II where Italian uses the congiuntivo imperfetto or trapassato: se studiassi = wenn ich studierte, se avessi studiato = wenn ich studiert hätte."
